atlas substrate
# The 14 Reality Foundry substrates. Constitutional restriction (atlas README):
# a substrate OWNS MECHANICS. It may not inherit the semantics of the
# architectures that ride it. AuthorityGraph and WorkGraph may both serialize
# through the same store; their algebras stay distinct. Every entry states that
# as a forbidden_inference. Maturity is honest: HVM4 and YaFF are witnessed by
# real runs/tests in this repo; the other 12 are declared -- their Reality
# Foundry role is a contract, and each names the exact witness that graduates it
# to implemented. None is laundered to measured without that witness.

architecture yaff
  canonical_name YaFF
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What is the semantic contract for a trial's artifacts, effects, and expected witnesses?
  purpose Semantic contract / IR for the trial: artifacts, effects, expected witnesses.
  maturity implemented
  internal_calculus block-and-field contract representation
  invariant a contract representation owns encoding, not the meaning of what it encodes
  forbidden_inference two architectures sharing YaFF -> the same semantics
  native_format yaff
  source_path architecture/atlas.py
  source_path schemas/control
  witness architecture/tests/test_atlas.py
  witness packs
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate

architecture hvm4
  canonical_name HVM4
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What is the bounded reduction of this selected symbolic or computational structure?
  purpose Bounded recursive reduction of selected symbolic/computational structures.
  maturity implemented
  internal_calculus interaction-net reduction
  invariant owns reduction mechanics, not the meaning of the structure reduced
  forbidden_inference a reduction completing -> the reduced structure is correct
  native_format helix
  interacts fpq-seed
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/substrate_hvm.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_substrate_hvm.py
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap installed binary is HVM2 (2.0.22); HVM4 upgrade + hvm-lang front-end still pending

architecture automerge
  canonical_name Automerge
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question How do many agents and humans mutate candidate state without contaminating Actual?
  purpose Collaborative candidate state; Possible may be mutated freely without touching Actual.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus CRDT merge mechanics
  invariant owns conflict-free merge, not the meaning of any candidate it holds
  forbidden_inference a candidate merged in Possible -> a change to Actual
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Automerge CRDT merge runs on candidate state in-repo with a test

architecture feldera
  canonical_name Feldera
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What are the incremental consequences of a change to events, tests, CMS, ledgers, or form readiness?
  purpose Incremental maintenance of consequences over GitHub events, test results, CMS changes, ledger updates, form readiness, live queries.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus incremental view maintenance
  invariant owns incremental recomputation, not the semantics of the views maintained
  forbidden_inference a maintained view -> authority over what it summarizes
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Feldera/DBSP incremental view runs over live events with a test

architecture egglog
  canonical_name egglog
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What are the equivalent alternatives to this plan, rewrite, representation, or composition?
  purpose Equivalence search over execution plans, rewrites, data representations, API compositions, patch transformations.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus e-graph equality saturation
  invariant owns equivalence-search machinery, not the correctness of a chosen alternative
  forbidden_inference two forms found equivalent by search -> equivalent under every architecture's algebra
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real egglog rewrite runs in the composition path with a test

architecture gigatoken
  canonical_name GigaToken
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question From the giant source, what purpose-specific mission context should be compiled?
  purpose Giant-source/context substrate from which purpose-specific mission contexts are compiled. The token/context-reduction engine.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus high-throughput token substrate + context compilation
  invariant owns context compilation, not the sufficiency of a compiled cut
  forbidden_inference a compiled context -> all evidence the mission needs is present
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when GigaToken compiles a real mission context with a witness

architecture lance
  canonical_name Lance
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question Where is the multimodal/vector body of code, traces, docs, images, transcripts, review artifacts?
  purpose Multimodal / vector body for code, traces, docs, images, transcripts, review artifacts.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus columnar vector storage + ANN index
  invariant owns vector storage, not the identity or authority of what is embedded
  forbidden_inference vector similarity -> same actor or same claim
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Lance vector store is written and queried in-repo with a test

architecture daft
  canonical_name Daft
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question How are large mixed-data transformations run across these corpora?
  purpose Large mixed-data transformations across the corpora.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus distributed dataframe execution
  invariant owns bulk transformation, not the provenance of its inputs or outputs
  forbidden_inference a transformed corpus -> provenance preserved without a witness
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Daft transformation runs over a corpus with a test

architecture tract
  canonical_name Tract
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What is the lightweight local model execution phenotype?
  purpose Lightweight local model execution phenotype.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus local inference runtime
  invariant an execution phenotype, not a model identity or representation
  forbidden_inference runs locally -> the representation it runs is authorized or correct
  interacts kv-temporal
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when Tract runs a real local model inference with a test

architecture burn
  canonical_name Burn
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What is the trainable tensor/model phenotype?
  purpose Trainable tensor/model phenotype.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus autodiff training runtime
  invariant a training phenotype, not the identity of the model trained
  forbidden_inference trained -> generation quality good (the FPQ lesson generalizes)
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Burn training/inference step runs with a test

architecture cubecl
  canonical_name CubeCL
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question When a learned or fused operation warrants it, what is the accelerated generated-kernel phenotype?
  purpose Accelerated generated-kernel phenotype where a learned/fused operation warrants it.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus generated GPU kernels
  invariant owns kernel generation, not the correctness of the fused operation
  forbidden_inference a generated kernel is fast -> the fused operation is valid
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real generated CubeCL kernel executes with a test

architecture hydro
  canonical_name Hydro
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What is the distributed placement/dataflow phenotype for this work?
  purpose Distributed placement / dataflow phenotype.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus distributed dataflow placement
  invariant a placement phenotype, not the authority to run what it places
  forbidden_inference placeable -> authorized to execute there
  interacts service-lifecycle
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Hydro dataflow places and runs work with a test

architecture restate
  canonical_name Restate
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question How does the trial durably wait hours or days on external reality?
  purpose Durable long-lived execution when the trial waits on external reality.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus durable execution + journaling
  invariant owns durability, not the meaning of the work it keeps alive
  forbidden_inference durably waiting -> the external event will occur
  interacts work-graph
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Restate durable execution journals a long wait with a test

architecture verus
  canonical_name Verus
  family substrate
  domain Reality Foundry
  layer substrate
  semantic_question Which invariants are worth proving, and does the proof hold within bounds?
  purpose Bounded formal verification for invariants worth proving.
  maturity declared
  internal_calculus bounded SMT verification
  invariant a proof of a stated invariant is not a proof of an unstated one
  forbidden_inference one invariant proven -> the system is correct
  native_format crux
  interacts proof-frontier
  source_lineage Reality Foundry 14-substrate
  known_gap graduates when a real Verus proof of a named invariant passes with the proof artifact as witness
